<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Did the Trail Blazers Extend Ja Morant?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Morant is paid <strong>$42.17m</strong> because a second overall pick who earns the designated rookie tag is paid a set share of the cap, and the salary rises every year of the deal.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went second in 2019 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$39.62m</strong>.</li>
<li>Memphis exercised both options on it, in 2021 and 2022.</li>
<li>The extension is <strong>$197.23m</strong> over five years, fully guaranteed.</li>
<li>It carries a 15% trade bonus.</li>
<li>His salary went from <strong>$12.12m</strong> to <strong>$34.01m</strong> in one year.</li>
</ul>
<p>He is the only Portland player earning more than <strong>$40m</strong> this season.</p>

