<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/ja-morant/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/ja-morant/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Are the Trail Blazers Paying Ja Morant in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Morant earns $42.17m in 2026-27, the largest salary at Portland and the last year of a five-year extension. It rises from $39.45m last season. His career earnings come to $191.96m across eight seasons. The salary is 21.98% of the club’s $191.82m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Ja Morant Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The contract ends after this season and he reaches free agency in 2028 at 28. All of the $197.23m was guaranteed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Ja Morant Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $42.17m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Does Ja Morant’s Contract With the Trail Blazers Include?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Morant signed a five-year extension worth $197.23m with Memphis in 2022 under the designated rookie rules, all of it guaranteed, with a 15% trade bonus. Portland took it on when it traded for him. The deal was written to pay $192.2m without an All-NBA selection and $231.4m with one. He reaches free agency in 2028 at 28."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Ja Morant’s Estimated Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Morant has a published net worth of around $50m, against $191.96m in career salary. He has endorsement income on top, which a figure like this is meant to include. He played two seasons at Murray State and Memphis took him second overall in 2019, two months before he turned 20."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Did the Trail Blazers Extend Ja Morant?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Morant is paid $42.17m because a second overall pick who earns the designated rookie tag is paid a set share of the cap, and the salary rises every year of the deal. He is the only Portland player earning more than $40m this season."}}]}</script>
